  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 281,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month to 1,180-1,260/month starting August 2026 (E-05), not from slow handling (within SLA, E-01) or a tariff change (none occurred, E-04). For 1,184 of 1,240 disputed ESTIMATED-read accounts, AMI reads were received and exported but rejected at billing import under rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01, E-13), which compares raw register values to 12-month m3 history with unit_scaling='none'; because v4.2-firmware meters (rollout 2026-06) record in 0.1 m3 units rather than m3 (E-14), their reads appear roughly 10x too high and are spuriously flagged high-consumption, forcing estimate substitution (E-12). This confirmed mechanism does not yet explain the majority of disputes (1,785 of 3,025, ACTUAL-read bills, E-03)."
 },
